From be1a81b2ba1f4195c4cd30f737d3c839114e54f2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jr31415 <jacob@rosen4.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 22:23:46 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 06/10] Frontend: opt-in threaded presenter (emulation+audio
 worker, vsync on main)

NDS_THREADED_PRESENT=1 runs the unchanged emulation loop on a worker thread
and keeps SDL events and the vsync'd present on the main thread. The loop is
no longer locked to the display rate, so a missed vblank or a long present no
longer starves the audio queue. Input arrives via a queue; the few
main-thread-only SDL calls go through run_on_main(). Default stays
single-threaded.

Measured cause (real session, 4374 frames): emulation p99 8.6 ms, 111 audio
underruns, mean frame 17.2 ms vs 16.7 ms DS period with present stalls to 138 ms.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
